              "source": "https://github.com/openrobokit/robokit/blob/main/src/robokit/robo/robot.py#L397",
              "doc": "<p>Compute the whole-body center of mass in world frame into <code>state.com_world</code>.</p><h4>Example</h4><div class=\"doc__code\" data-copy-scope><div class=\"bar\"><span style=\"color:var(--fg-dim)\">python</span><span class=\"code-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-toggle\" data-code-toggle aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Show full code\">Full</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy copy--swap\" data-copy-from=\"[data-code-full]\" title=\"Copy\"><span class=\"t\"></span><span class=\"o\"></span></button></span></div><pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; from robot_descriptions.loaders.yourdfpy import load_robot_description\n&gt;&gt;&gt; robot = Robot.load(load_robot_description(\"panda_description\"))\n&gt;&gt;&gt; state = robot.compute_center_of_mass(robot.state())\n&gt;&gt;&gt; np.allclose(state.com_world.numpy()[0], [0.0232, 0.0061, 0.6062], atol=1e-4)\nTrue</pre><pre data-code-full hidden>import numpy as np\nfrom robokit.robo.robot import Robot\n\nfrom robot_descriptions.loaders.yourdfpy import load_robot_description\nrobot = Robot.load(load_robot_description(\"panda_description\"))\nstate = robot.compute_center_of_mass(robot.state())\nnp.allclose(state.com_world.numpy()[0], [0.0232, 0.0061, 0.6062], atol=1e-4)</pre></div>",
