          "anchor": "gaussiansamplerconfig",
          "doc": "<p>Gaussian draw/update settings, independent of runtime population buffers.</p><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"doc__code\" data-copy-scope><div class=\"bar\"><span style=\"color:var(--fg-dim)\">python</span><span class=\"code-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-toggle\" data-code-toggle aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Show full code\">Full</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy copy--swap\" data-copy-from=\"[data-code-full]\" title=\"Copy\"><span class=\"t\"></span><span class=\"o\"></span></button></span></div><pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; from robokit.opt.var_values import VectorVar\n&gt;&gt;&gt; class Key(Enum):\n...     X = 0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; var = VarValues({Key.X: VectorVar(wp.zeros((1, 2), dtype=wp.float32, device=\"cpu\"))})\n&gt;&gt;&gt; config = GaussianSamplerConfig(var_key=Key.X, num_draws=8)\n&gt;&gt;&gt; first, second = config.build(var, 1), config.build(var, 1)\n&gt;&gt;&gt; first is second\nFalse\n&gt;&gt;&gt; first.noise.shape\n(8, 2)</pre><pre data-code-full hidden>import warp as wp\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom robokit.opt.sampler import GaussianSamplerConfig\nfrom robokit.opt.var_values import VarValues\n\nfrom robokit.opt.var_values import VectorVar\nclass Key(Enum):\n    X = 0\nvar = VarValues({Key.X: VectorVar(wp.zeros((1, 2), dtype=wp.float32, device=\"cpu\"))})\nconfig = GaussianSamplerConfig(var_key=Key.X, num_draws=8)\nfirst, second = config.build(var, 1), config.build(var, 1)\nfirst is second\nfirst.noise.shape</pre></div>",
