              "doc": "<p>Return the <code>Context</code> members a template reads, including those of the tasks it wraps.</p><h4>Example</h4><div class=\"doc__code\" data-copy-scope><div class=\"bar\"><span style=\"color:var(--fg-dim)\">python</span><span class=\"code-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-toggle\" data-code-toggle aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Show full code\">Full</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy copy--swap\" data-copy-from=\"[data-code-full]\" title=\"Copy\"><span class=\"t\"></span><span class=\"o\"></span></button></span></div><pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; class Inputs(Context):\n...     STEP = 0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; class Step(Task):\n...     def __init__(self, dt):\n...         self.dt = dt\n&gt;&gt;&gt; Step(dt=(Inputs.STEP, 2.0)).needs() == {Inputs.STEP}\nTrue</pre><pre data-code-full hidden>from robokit.terms.task import Context, Task\n\nclass Inputs(Context):\n    STEP = 0\nclass Step(Task):\n    def __init__(self, dt):\n        self.dt = dt\nStep(dt=(Inputs.STEP, 2.0)).needs() == {Inputs.STEP}</pre></div>",
