              "doc": "<p>Return [K,T,J] paths, preserving alternative initial pose hypotheses; each initial hypothesis retains a distinct branch, and the output contains at most <code>count</code> paths; periodic joints use angular distances and return continuous equivalent angles within supplied limits; if no continuous lift fits the limits, the original bounded path is retained.</p><div class=\"doc__code\" data-copy-scope><div class=\"bar\"><span style=\"color:var(--fg-dim)\">python</span><span class=\"code-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-toggle\" data-code-toggle aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Show full code\">Full</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy copy--swap\" data-copy-from=\"[data-code-full]\" title=\"Copy\"><span class=\"t\"></span><span class=\"o\"></span></button></span></div><pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; q = np.array([[[0.], [3.]], [[3.], [0.1]], [[0.2], [3.]]])\n&gt;&gt;&gt; TrajectorySmoothnessTask().compute_paths(q, np.array([[0., .1], [.1, 0.], [0., .1]]), np.arange(3.)).ravel().tolist()\n[0.0, 0.1, 0.2]</pre><pre data-code-full hidden>import numpy as np\nfrom robokit.terms.sparse.trajectory_smoothness_task import TrajectorySmoothnessTask\n\nq = np.array([[[0.], [3.]], [[3.], [0.1]], [[0.2], [3.]]])\nTrajectorySmoothnessTask().compute_paths(q, np.array([[0., .1], [.1, 0.], [0., .1]]), np.arange(3.)).ravel().tolist()</pre></div>",
