              "source": "https://github.com/openrobokit/robokit/blob/main/src/robokit/terms/task.py#L41",
              "doc": "<p>Swap each <code>Context</code> placeholder, alone or in a tuple, for its value; subclasses then build for the variable.</p><h4>Example</h4><div class=\"doc__code\" data-copy-scope><div class=\"bar\"><span style=\"color:var(--fg-dim)\">python</span><span class=\"code-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-toggle\" data-code-toggle aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Show full code\">Full</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy copy--swap\" data-copy-from=\"[data-code-full]\" title=\"Copy\"><span class=\"t\"></span><span class=\"o\"></span></button></span></div><pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; class Inputs(Context):\n...     STEP = 0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; class Step(Task):\n...     def __init__(self, dt):\n...         self.dt = dt\n&gt;&gt;&gt; task = Step(dt=(Inputs.STEP, 2.0))\n&gt;&gt;&gt; task.resolve(None, {Inputs.STEP: 0.5})  # the base swaps placeholders only\n&gt;&gt;&gt; task.dt\n(0.5, 2.0)</pre><pre data-code-full hidden>from robokit.terms.task import Context, Task\n\nclass Inputs(Context):\n    STEP = 0\nclass Step(Task):\n    def __init__(self, dt):\n        self.dt = dt\ntask = Step(dt=(Inputs.STEP, 2.0))\ntask.resolve(None, {Inputs.STEP: 0.5})  # the base swaps placeholders only\ntask.dt</pre></div>",
